About Nebius:

Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.

Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.

Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.

The role

Nebius is looking for a Senior Product Marketing Manager, focusing on Data Center &amp; Infrastructure, to own how Nebius talks about its infrastructure layer, from data centers and racks, to power and sustainability, and engage the local communities where we build. At the core of this role, is partnering with other Nebius teams, such as public affairs, government and investor relations, to navigate local political and regulatory dynamics, and address community concerns openly. You’re welcome to work remotely in the United States.

Nebius's advantage starts in the physical world: in our data centers, our custom servers with NVIDIA GPUs and networking fabric we operate. As we build new sites across the US and beyond, we need someone who can tell that story with credibility and heart: to customers and analysts, to investors and press, and to the communities where our data centers are built. &nbsp;

This role sits at the intersection of technical storytelling, infrastructure fluency, and community trust. You are as comfortable explaining a liquid-cooled GPU rack as you are sitting in a town hall, and you can move between the two without losing either audience. &nbsp;

Reporting to the Product Marketing Lead, you'll work hand in hand with our engineering and product management organization, data center operations, Sustainability, Communications, and Public Affairs / Government Relations teams. &nbsp;

Your responsibilities will include: &nbsp;

• Own the infrastructure and data center narrative. Translate Nebius's &nbsp;vertically integrated, energy -to- API advantage : turn our c ustom hardware, NVIDIA GPU platforms, high-performance networking fabric, storage, power, and cooling into clear, credible messaging for technical and business audiences. Contribute to our overall Nebius core messaging, positioning and story. &nbsp;

• Lead the local community engagement for new and existing data center builds. This is the heart of the role and you will need to p artner with our local site , public affairs and government relations to campaign positively around new US (and global) data center initiatives . You will d evelop community-facing materials as required , such as fact sheets, FAQs, town-hall content, local economic-impact and jobs stories that address concerns about energy, grid, water, noise, and land honestly and proactively. &nbsp;

• Enable go-to-market and field teams. Arm sales, solutions, and partner teams with the messaging and assets they need to sell the infrastructure story . From first-call decks, battlecards, discovery guides, ROI/TCO tools, objection handling, and competitive positioning against hyperscalers and neoclouds. Run enablement sessions and measure whether the field is adopting and winning with what you build. &nbsp;

• Tell the efficiency and sustainability story. Turn energy efficiency, power and cooling design, heat reuse, water stewardship, renewable sourcing, and sustainability metrics into proof points that stand up to scrutiny from customers, investors, regulators, and communities alike. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Evangelize our GPU platform layer . Work closely with Nebius's &nbsp;product management , engineering teams , and our NVIDIA counterparts

